  const ExpenseState({this.expenses = const []});
  this.expenses = const [] is the default value.
  If nobody passes a list, expenses becomes an empty list. 
  Default values in Dart must be compile-time constants, 
  which is why it says const [] and not just []. 
  A const list is  unmodifiable: if you call .add() on it, the app throws an error at runtime.
